# The board and its rules
// American checkers:  8 by 8, each side's 12 pieces on the dark squares of its first three rows.
// A piece moves one square on a diagonal, forward only, until it reaches the far row and is crowned a king:
// a king moves forward and back.
// A piece jumps an enemy piece next to it, onto the empty square beyond, and takes it;
// a jump must be taken when there is one, and a piece that jumps carries on jumping while it can.
// Black moves first.  A side with no pieces left, or no move to make, has lost.

a "piece" is a draggable view
	-- A checker:  a man, until it reaches the far row and is crowned a king.
	its "side" is one of black or red
	its "rank" is one of man or king
	it "is a king" if its rank is king
	its "forward" is
		-- Which way down the board it moves:  black up, from the bottom;  red down, from the top
		-1 if its side is black
		1 otherwise
	its "far row" is
		1 if its side is black
		8 otherwise

a "square" is a viewable, droppable list of pieces
	-- One of the board's 64, by its row and column:  row 1 at the top, column 1 on the left.
	-- Only the 32 dark ones are played on;  each holds one piece, or none.
	its "row" is a number
	its "column" is a number
	its "shade" is one of light or dark
		-- set as the board is made:  dark where its row and column add up to an odd number
	its "piece" is the first piece in it

a piece belongs to one square

a "board" is a viewable list of squares
	-- The 64 squares, a game on them, and whose turn it is
	its "turn" is one of black or red
	its "winner" is one of nobody, black or red
	its "turned" is yes or no
		-- Drawn turned round, red's side nearest:  the other player's view of the same game
	its "picked piece" is a piece
		-- The piece clicked, to move with the next click
	its "jumper" is a piece
		-- The piece in the middle of jumps:  only it may move, and only to jump again
	it "is over" if its winner is not nobody

	when creating a board
		for row from 1 to 8
			for column from 1 to 8
				set shade to dark if row + column is in [3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15] otherwise light
				add a new square with row, column and shade to the board

a square belongs to one board

group "Finding Squares"

to "the square at (row as a number) and (column as a number) on (a board)"
	-- nothing off the board's edge
	if row < 1 or row > 8
		return nothing
	if column < 1 or column > 8
		return nothing
	set index to row * 8 - 8 + column
	return item index of the board


group "Moves"

a piece
	it "can jump to (a square)" if
		-- Two squares on along a diagonal, forward unless it's a king, over an enemy piece onto an empty square
		set rows to the row of the square - the row of its square
		set columns to the column of the square - the column of its square
		if the absolute value of rows is not 2 or the absolute value of columns is not 2 or the square is not empty
			return no
		if it is not a king and rows * its forward < 0
			return no
		set row to (the row of its square + the row of the square) / 2
		set column to (the column of its square + the column of the square) / 2
		set middle to the square at row and column on the board of its square
		set enemy to the piece of middle
		return enemy exists and the side of enemy is not its side

	it "has a jump" if
		-- Whether there's a square it can jump to
		return the board of its square has squares where the piece can jump to it

a board
	it "is forced to jump" if
		-- Whether the side whose turn it is has a jump to make:  then it must make one
		return it has squares where its piece exists and the side of its piece is the turn of the board and its piece has a jump

a piece
	it "can go to (a square)" if
		-- Whether it's a move the rules allow:  a step, or a jump when it must
		if the shade of the square is light or the square is not empty
			return no
		set board to the board of its square
		if the board is over or its side is not the turn of the board
			return no
		if the jumper of the board exists and it is not the jumper of the board
			return no
		set rows to the row of the square - the row of its square
		set columns to the column of the square - the column of its square
		if it is not a king and rows * its forward < 0
			return no
		if the absolute value of rows is 2 and the absolute value of columns is 2
			return it can jump to the square
		if the absolute value of rows is 1 and the absolute value of columns is 1
			return the jumper of the board does not exist and the board is not forced to jump
		return no

	it "can move" if
		-- Whether there's a square it can go to
		return the board of its square has squares where the piece can go to it

	its "letter" is
		-- How the board's diagram writes it:  b and r for each side's men, B and R for its kings
		"B" if its side is black and it is a king
		"b" if its side is black
		"R" if it is a king
		"r" otherwise

a board
	it "has a move" if
		-- Whether the side whose turn it is can move at all:  with none, it has lost
		return it has squares where its piece exists and its piece can move

	its "diagram" is
		-- Each square's piece as a letter, top left to bottom right:  "" for an empty one
		set letters to a new list of text
		for square in the board
			add (the letter of the piece of the square if the square is not empty otherwise "") to letters
		return letters

group "Playing"

to "reset (a board)"
	-- No pieces on it, black to move, and nobody's won
	for square in the board
		empty the square
	set the turn of the board to black
	set the winner of the board to nobody
	set the jumper of the board to nothing
	set the picked piece of the board to nothing

to "start a new game on (a board)"
	-- Each side's 12 men on the dark squares of its first three rows, black to move
	reset the board
	for square in the board where its shade is dark
		if the row of the square < 4
			add a new piece with side red and rank man to the square
		if the row of the square > 5
			add a new piece with side black and rank man to the square

to "set up (a board) from (diagram as a list)"
	-- Every square's piece as the diagram says (`its diagram`):  black to move, and nobody's won
	reset the board
	for square, index in the board
		set letter to item index of diagram
		if letter is "b" or letter is "B"
			add a new piece with side black to the square
		if letter is "r" or letter is "R"
			add a new piece with side red to the square
		if letter is "B" or letter is "R"
			set the rank of the piece of the square to king

a board
	its "jump square" is
		-- Where its jumper is, by the square's place on the board, 1 to 64:  0 while no piece is jumping
		0 if its jumper does not exist
		the position of the square of its jumper in it otherwise

to "copy (a board) onto (other as a board)"
	-- The other board shows the same game:  its pieces, whose turn it is, who's won, and which piece is jumping
	set up other from the diagram of the board
	set the turn of other to the turn of the board
	set the winner of other to the winner of the board
	if the jump square of the board > 0
		set the jumper of other to the piece of (item (the jump square of the board) of other)

to move (a piece) to (a square)
	-- The piece onto the square, if the rules let it:  a jump takes the piece it jumps
	-- - then it's crowned on the far row, or jumps again while it can, or the other side's turn comes
	cancel if the piece cannot go to the square
	set board to the board of the square
	set start to the square of the piece
	set jumped to the absolute value of (the row of the square - the row of start) is 2
	if jumped
		set middle to the square at (the row of start + the row of the square) / 2 and (the column of start + the column of the square) / 2 on board
		empty middle
		play "piece take"
	otherwise
		play "piece down"
	add the piece to the square
	set the picked piece of board to nothing
	if the piece is not a king and the row of the square is the far row of the piece
		set the rank of the piece to king
		play "level up"
		end the turn on board
	otherwise if jumped and the piece has a jump
		set the jumper of board to the piece
	otherwise
		end the turn on board

to "end the turn on (a board)"
	-- The other side's turn:  with no piece that can move, it has lost
	set the jumper of the board to nothing
	set the turn of the board to red if the turn of the board is black otherwise black
	if the board does not have a move
		set the winner of the board to red if the turn of the board is black otherwise black

group "Tests"

to "put a (side as text) (rank as text) at (row as a number) and (column as a number) on (a board)"
	-- One piece on a square, for a test to set up the position it wants
	add a new piece with side and rank to the square at row and column on the board

to test the opening
	set board to a new board
	start a new game on board
	the number of squares in board where it is not empty should be 24
	the turn of board should be black
	set man to the piece of (the square at 6 and 1 on board)
	the side of man should be black
	man can go to (the square at 5 and 2 on board) should be yes
	man can go to (the square at 7 and 2 on board) should be no
	man can go to (the square at 4 and 3 on board) should be no
	-- red waits its turn
	the piece of (the square at 3 and 2 on board) can move should be no
	move man to the square at 5 and 2 on board
	the turn of board should be red

to test a jump must be taken
	set board to a new board
	reset board
	put a "black" "man" at 6 and 3 on board
	put a "red" "man" at 5 and 4 on board
	put a "black" "man" at 6 and 7 on board
	board is forced to jump should be yes
	-- a step isn't allowed while there's a jump to make
	the piece of (the square at 6 and 7 on board) can go to (the square at 5 and 6 on board) should be no
	set jumper to the piece of (the square at 6 and 3 on board)
	jumper can go to (the square at 5 and 2 on board) should be no
	jumper can go to (the square at 4 and 5 on board) should be yes
	move jumper to the square at 4 and 5 on board
	the square at 5 and 4 on board is empty should be yes
	-- red has no pieces left:  black wins
	the winner of board should be black

to test jumping on
	set board to a new board
	reset board
	put a "black" "man" at 7 and 2 on board
	put a "red" "man" at 6 and 3 on board
	put a "red" "man" at 4 and 5 on board
	put a "red" "man" at 1 and 8 on board
	set jumper to the piece of (the square at 7 and 2 on board)
	move jumper to the square at 5 and 4 on board
	-- still black's turn:  the same piece jumps again
	the turn of board should be black
	the jumper of board should be jumper
	move jumper to the square at 3 and 6 on board
	the number of squares in board where it is not empty should be 2
	the turn of board should be red
	the winner of board should be nobody

to test crowning a king
	set board to a new board
	reset board
	put a "black" "man" at 2 and 3 on board
	put a "red" "man" at 5 and 8 on board
	set man to the piece of (the square at 2 and 3 on board)
	move man to the square at 1 and 2 on board
	man is a king should be yes
	the turn of board should be red
	move the piece of (the square at 5 and 8 on board) to the square at 6 and 7 on board
	-- a king moves back down the board
	man can go to (the square at 2 and 3 on board) should be yes

to test the diagram
	set board to a new board
	start a new game on board
	set other to a new board
	set up other from the diagram of board
	the diagram of other as text should be the diagram of board as text
	the number of squares in other where it is not empty should be 24
	move the piece of (the square at 6 and 1 on board) to the square at 5 and 2 on board
	copy board onto other
	the diagram of other as text should be the diagram of board as text
	the turn of other should be red
